# T-078: the page a shared comparison opens. The ZIP and the plan IDs are IN the path, so the
# link is readable and nothing is stored on a server; a 200 rewrite keeps that URL in the address
# bar and serves one file, which then reads the ZIP and the IDs back out of location.pathname.
# Two things this line has already got wrong once each, both found on the staging preview:
#   * the destination must be EXTENSIONLESS. Pages redirects /x.html to /x, so a rewrite that
#     targets the .html file turns into a 308 and the readable link is lost;
#   * the file must not be named after the path. An asset called opciones.html makes /opciones a
#     route and every deeper path 308s back to it, before this rule is ever consulted.
# Status 200, never 404: Cloudflare Pages silently drops 404 rules.
/opciones/*              /opciones-compartidas   200

